          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to protest, then the Marathi for to boycott."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सत्ता",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सत्ता — sattā — \"power (political)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सत्ता हातात आली की माणूस बदलतो. sattā hātāt ālī kī māṇūs badalto. When power comes into his hands, a man changes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सत्तेवर येणे, to come to power."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सत्ता (sattā) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit sattā, \"existence, being\" (Monier-Williams). Marathi uses it for the power to rule."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
